     Better be careful with such accusations, because it _can_ be
possible depending on the configuration used to compile the game.
The field for storing the enchantment value is normally 8 bits,
allowing -128 through +127, but some compilers don't handle that
well and NetHack has to be configured for them to use 16 bits instead.
(And anyone could deliberately configure it to use 32 bits, or perhaps
even 64 bits on an Alpha or other super-duper new CPU, although why
anyone would want to bother doing that is beyond me.)

